      "sourceHold": "M14-private-source-hold",
      "sourceTermFace": {
        "japanese": "それから",
        "english": "then"
      },
      "entryKind": "lesson-sense-context-link",
      "contextualGlossEnglish": "then, introducing the next action in a sequence",
      "explanationEnglish": "それから connects one action to the next in time and means 'then'. In this turn it links eating breakfast to going to work. It expresses order, not cause.",
      "readerExample": {
        "sourceKind": "dialogue",
        "japanese": "それから、しごとに いきます。",
        "english": "Then I go to work.",
        "sourceTurnOneBased": 4,
        "selectedJapanese": null,
        "audioScript": null,
        "reviewed": false
      },
      "usageNoteEnglish": "In this source それから opens the sentence, is followed by a comma, and comes after a まず sentence. It is a different word from そのあと in turn 14 (そのあと えきに つきました。), which the source renders as 'After that'.",
      "internalQuestions": [
        "Existing rows ja-en-492f5ae9f19d00aa (after that) and ja-en-c24ce926e407d2a0 (then) are distinct records in pinned main. Preserve both; this exact-face proposal references then only. No merge, split or ownership selection is performed."
      ],
      "explanationJapanese": "まえの うごきの あとに、つぎの うごきを つなぐ ことばです。「それから、しごとに いきます。」では、あさごはんを たべた あとに しごとに いく ことを しめします。りゆうを あらわす ことばでは ありません。",
